<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <Itf Name="I_PositioningAxis" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000001}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    The drive contract a shuttle axis is commanded through: power, an absolute
    target, an acknowledgement, and the position feedback a sequencer needs to
    know whether it has arrived.

    A belt drive is asked how FAST it is going; a shuttle axis is asked WHERE
    it is. That is the whole difference between this contract and the velocity
    one a conveyor run uses, and it is why the horizontal and vertical axes of
    the mover are the same block twice rather than a special case of the belt.

    A consumer commands EVERY scan. MoveAbsolute is a level, not a one-shot:
    the equipment module re-asserts its target each cycle, so a drive that
    resets, or a link that drops and returns, converges back on the commanded
    position instead of waiting for a fresh edge.

    InPosition is a COMPARISON, not a latch, and a consumer may rely on that.
    Commanding a new target drops it in the same call, so a sequencer that
    changes target and then reads InPosition on the same scan cannot be told it
    has arrived at somewhere it has not yet set off for.
*)
INTERFACE I_PositioningAxis]]></Declaration>
    <Method Name="Enable" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000002}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Requests drive power. Returns whether the drive is live yet, which is not
// the same as the request having been accepted, so a caller that needs power
// re-asserts rather than assuming.
METHOD Enable : BOOL]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="MoveAbsolute" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000003}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD MoveAbsolute : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	// Target in mm on this axis' own reference, which is the same reference
	// the position table is surveyed in.
	Position : LREAL;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Reset" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000004}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Acknowledges a drive fault. Clears Error only if whatever raised it has
// gone away; a standing fault survives the acknowledgement.
METHOD Reset : BOOL]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="Error" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000005}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A drive-side fault is standing. Held until Reset is called AND the cause
// has cleared, so a consumer may treat it as a level rather than an event.
PROPERTY Error : BOOL]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000006}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="ActualPosition" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000007}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Measured position in the same units MoveAbsolute is commanded in.
PROPERTY ActualPosition : LREAL]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000008}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="CommandedPosition" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-000000000009}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The target the axis is currently working towards. Readable so that a
// coordinated move can be observed as coordinated: an axis carrying its
// target while another axis is the one still travelling is the difference
// between two axes moving together and two moving one after the other.
PROPERTY CommandedPosition : LREAL]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-00000000000a}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="InPosition" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-00000000000b}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The axis is standing within its in-position window of the commanded target.
// False on an unpowered or faulted drive whatever the encoder says, because
// an axis nobody is holding is not standing anywhere on purpose.
PROPERTY InPosition : BOOL]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{5e4501d0-0034-4d19-9a41-00000000000c}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
  </Itf>
</TcPlcObject>
